fsck: check for stale stripe needs_reconcile flags

needs_reconcile on a stripe means a block sits on a bad/evacuating device
and the stripe needs repair. But the flag is only ever cleared by
rewriting the stripe, which bch2_stripe_repair() only does for stripes
that are still degraded: a stripe flagged during a transient device state
(device marked evacuating, then returned to rw) keeps the flag forever.

At runtime this makes every reconcile pass reprocess the stripe - ret == 0,
no IO, no state change - spinning reconcile_hipri indefinitely while real
work (data pending, EC conversion) starves behind it. Observed on a
10-device pool: ~445k flagged stripes, reconcile_stripe counter in the
petabytes, zero bytes moved.

check_reconcile_work already validates the other direction
(stripe_needs_reconcile_not_set); make it bidirectional: a flagged stripe
whose blocks are all on healthy devices has the flag cleared. Runs in the
existing stripes walk, alongside check_stripe_can_widen_one(). New error
stripe_needs_reconcile_stale, marked FSCK_AUTOFIX.

Exports bch2_stripe_degraded() (was static stripe_degraded() in
fs/data/ec/create.c) for the check.

